      "number": 6,
      "id": "I_kwDOTu3Wf88AAAABYxi-dg",
      "title": "Should the dialog lifecycle be added in the architecture document?",
      "url": "https://github.com/zaheduzzaman/overall-aiproto-architecture/issues/6",
      "state": "OPEN",
      "author": "zaheduzzaman",
      "authorAssociation": "OWNER",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "As terminology section defines dialog, context etc. It seems we could describe the dialog context lifecycle, however, this could be also described in the protocol document where the will be more discussions on the lifecycle states and interaction. ",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-21T09:01:34Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-22T12:21:40Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "comments": [
        {
          "author": "zaheduzzaman",
          "authorAssociation": "OWNER",
          "body": "The thing is the dialog context lifecycle needs to be discussed to agree upon the states and transitions. We can now add the lifecycle into the architecture document now and start the discussion. Later we can decide whether it should be part of the architecture or part of the protocol specification. As the protocol specification would also benefit from the lifecycle discussion, waiting for the protocol discussion may just delay the discussion.",
          "createdAt": "2026-10-22T12:21:39Z",
          "updatedAt": "2026-10-22T12:21:39Z"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
